# Email Campaign Measurement Plan

## Campaign Overview

This document outlines how the Noura Botanics welcome email sequence would be evaluated.

The campaign consists of three emails:

- Email 1: Welcome to Noura Botanics
- Email 2: A Little Reminder to Keep Skincare Simple
- Email 3: Three Products, That's It

As this is a hypothetical portfolio project, no actual campaign data or performance results are available.

## Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)

| Metric | What it measures |
|---|---|
| Open Rate | Percentage of delivered emails that are opened, where measurable |
| Click-Through Rate (CTR) | Percentage of delivered emails that receive at least one click |
| Click-to-Open Rate (CTOR) | Percentage of opened emails that receive a click |
| Conversion Rate | Percentage of recipients who complete the intended action |
| Unsubscribe Rate | Percentage of delivered emails that result in an unsubscribe |

## What I Would Measure

**Email 1 – Welcome**

- Whether subscribers engage with the welcome email
- Clicks on the "Explore the Collection" CTA

**Email 2 – Skincare Basics**

- Engagement with the educational content
- Clicks on the "Find Your Essentials" CTA

**Email 3 – Product Discovery**

- Clicks on individual product links, if available
- Clicks on the "See the Essentials" CTA
- Purchases attributed to the email, if tracking is available

## Evaluation Approach

I would compare the performance of each email to understand which type of content generates more engagement.

I would also review unsubscribe rates and conversions to identify whether the sequence is relevant to subscribers and supports the campaign objectives.

## Optimisation Opportunities

Based on the results, I would consider:

- Testing different subject lines.
- Reviewing CTA wording and placement.
- Adjusting the timing between emails.
- Improving product descriptions or email layouts if engagement is low.

## Important Note

All metrics listed above are proposed measurement criteria. No actual campaign results, subscriber data or sales figures have been generated.
